# Environment Variable Reference

Copy this file to `.env` in the repository root and fill in real values before running.
**Never commit your `.env` file — it is listed in `.gitignore`.**

```bash
cp .env.example .env
```

---

## Database

# PostgreSQL connection URL (used by chatai-backend)
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:CHANGE_ME_DB_PASSWORD@localhost:5432/chatai

# Individual components used by docker-compose
DB_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME_DB_PASSWORD
DB_PORT=5432

---

## Encryption & Internal Security

# Master AES-256-GCM key for the credential vault.
# MUST be at least 32 bytes. Generate with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# The application will refuse to start if this is missing or too short.
VAULT_ENCRYPTION_KEY=CHANGE_ME_minimum_32_bytes_hex_or_passphrase_here_pad_if_needed

# Shared cluster secret authenticating Node → Go → Python inter-service calls.
# Use a high-entropy random string (64+ chars recommended).
INTERNAL_SERVICE_SECRET=CHANGE_ME_high_entropy_cluster_token_64_chars_minimum

---

## Authentication (Supabase)

# Supabase project URL.
# For local development with a self-hosted Supabase: http://localhost:8000
# For Supabase Cloud: https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# Service role key (bypasses Row Level Security — keep this secret).
# Found in Supabase Dashboard → Settings → API → service_role
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...your_service_role_key

---

## LLM Provider API Keys
# These are optional. Users can supply their own keys (BYOK) via the dashboard.
# Keys set here serve as org-level defaults (encrypted in vault at runtime).

# OpenRouter (recommended — routes to many providers via one key)
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...

# OpenAI direct
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# Anthropic direct
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Google Gemini (via AI Studio)
GOOGLE_API_KEY=AIza...

---

## Billing & Payments (Optional — for SaaS deployments only)
# Self-hosted deployments do not require Stripe.

STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_live_...
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...

---

## Service Ports (Optional Overrides)
# These default to the values shown. Change only if you have port conflicts.

# NODE_PORT=5000
# GO_RUNTIME_PORT=8081
# PYTHON_BRAIN_PORT=8082

---

## Frontend (Next.js)
# Only needed if running the frontend separately from docker-compose.
# Point this at the Node.js backend.

NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:5000
